body:
The maintainer answered in chat on 2026-11-22: "I cannot give any of what you are asking for in #3319". The stock, tool and Lead in/out values of the operation, and a move dump, will not come.

Next step, without his data: one bounded search for the cause on `fig8.step` with `EM-0800-4FL` and the known heights (Clearance 32, Top 22, Bottom 1.5, Stepdown 10, Hop below clearance off). The worker changes one setting at a time and looks for any lateral rapid below the clearance plane, or a `RapidInStock` warning, on each generated program:
- the entry kind (Plunge, Helix, Ramp) and its parameters;
- the link settings of the Lead in / Lead out tab;
- the stock shape, size and offset, and the tool assembly (flute length, shank, holder);
- the finish and spring pass settings, the stepover and the containment.

The scout read of the planner (comment 7077519903) names the best candidate: the restart at the pass start in `ladder_links.rs:189-199`, which posts a vertical rapid after the lateral rapid at the clearance.

If the search finds a program that shows the defect, the worker pins it as a red test and fixes it (P1). If it finds nothing, the worker posts the table of what was tried. The issue then stays open and `blocked` until the maintainer decides on the priority.
